MERIDIAN SUPPLIER SERVICE AGREEMENT
Draft for AI Risk Review

Parties:
Meridian Holdings Ltd. ("Meridian")
Apex Facilities Services LLC ("Supplier")

Effective Date: March 1, 2024

1. Scope of Services
Supplier will provide emergency leak response, plumbing coordination, ceiling tile replacement, and facilities documentation for Meridian commercial properties.

2. Response Time
Supplier will use commercially reasonable efforts to respond to urgent water intrusion tickets within 72 hours. Supplier has no liability for delayed response unless Meridian separately approves emergency pricing in writing.

3. Indemnity
Tenant claims, property damage claims, business interruption claims, evidence preservation claims, and data-loss claims arising from water intrusion are the sole responsibility of the affected tenant. Supplier will indemnify Meridian only for direct physical damage caused by Supplier's gross negligence after written notice and a 30-day cure period.

4. Notice Logs
Supplier may maintain repair tickets in its internal portal. Meridian is not required to preserve Supplier portal records unless Meridian receives a litigation hold directly from outside counsel.

5. Limitation of Liability
Supplier's aggregate liability under this agreement is limited to the fees paid by Meridian during the 30 days before the event giving rise to the claim. Consequential damages, lost profits, loss of use, business interruption, and client-file damage are excluded.

6. Termination
Meridian may terminate this agreement at any time for convenience. Supplier may terminate only after 90 days written notice and only if all open work orders are complete.

7. Confidentiality
Supplier may not disclose maintenance tickets, tenant complaints, inspection photographs, or internal communications without Meridian's prior written consent.

AI REVIEW NOTES
- One-sided liability language could help explain why repair records are missing.
- Clause 4 creates a preservation risk for maintenance portal logs.
- Clause 5 excludes the same categories Marcus Chen is claiming as damages.
- Clause 7 may obstruct discovery if Meridian uses it to delay production.
